    statTrDatum:"Individual sessions by date", statBlocsTitel:"BLOCs over time", statBlocsSub:"the BLOCs you trained", statBlocN:"trained {n}×", statBlocZuletzt:"last {d}", statBlocsHinweis:"Volume = weight × repetitions of the working sets, compared between the first and the last of your last five sessions. A description only, not a rating; muscle groups, frequency and balance of the week are in Deep Dive.", ddKalBtn:"Add to calendar", ddKalWann:"On which day?", ddKalOk:"In calendar: {d}", ddHeute:"Today", ddMorgen:"Tomorrow", ddAnsehen:"View", ddFreqTitel:"How often per muscle group", ddFreq2:"On two days or more:", ddFreq1:"On one day only:", ddFreq0:"Not yet included:", ddKalTitel:"Your week at a glance", ddKalLegende:"Filled dot: trained · hollow dot: planned in the calendar · right: days this week", ddIst:"Trained", ddPlan:"With plan", ddBalTitel:"Balance", ddPush:"Push", ddPull:"Pull", ddOben:"Upper body", ddUnten:"Lower body", ddBalInfo:"Push: movements where you press a load away from your body, e.g. bench press, push-ups, shoulder press. Mainly works chest, front shoulder and triceps. Pull: movements where you pull a load toward your body, e.g. rows, pull-ups, lat pulldown. Mainly works back, rear shoulder and biceps. The balance shows how the exercises of your week split between both sides. Main muscles count fully, helper muscles 0.35. Upper and lower shows the same for upper and lower body. This is an overview, not a rating. A balanced ratio is a common practice rule, not a proven requirement.", ddBalHinweis:"Only describes how the week is distributed (main and assisting muscles of the exercises). A balanced ratio of pushing and pulling is a common rule of thumb, not an evidence-based requirement.", ddWho:"{n} of 6 muscle groups on at least 2 days. The WHO recommends muscle-strengthening for the major groups on at least 2 days a week; the progress tab counts strength days overall.", ddZuFortschritt:"See time, streak and trends over several weeks in Progress", statZuDeepDive:"See this week’s muscle groups, frequency and balance in Deep Dive", ddAnteil:"Share of muscle groups", ddLeerKal:"Nothing entered for this week yet. As soon as you train or plan workouts in the calendar, this overview fills up.", ddPlanenBtn:"Plan in calendar", exHistorie:"Last 30 days: trained {n} times · last {z}", exHeute:"today", exGestern:"yesterday", exVor:"{n} days ago", ddChipTrainings:"Workouts", ddChipZeit:"Time", ddChipUebungen:"Exercises", ddVerteilung:"Muscle group split", ddNaechstes:"Idea for your next session", ddZuKurz:"{g} was least represented this week", ddHinweis:"An overview only, not a rating. Percentages come from each exercise’s main muscles (counted fully) and assisting muscles (counted at 0.35); the numbers on the right show the change from last week in percentage points. A leg day stays a leg day.", ddWoche:"Per week", ddWorkout:"Per workout", ddDiese:"This week", ddLeer:"No training with exercises this week yet.", ddVor:"Previous week", ddNach:"Next week", progMeta:"{n} entries", progMeta1:"1 entry", progStartFehler:"The next entry could not start.", kalPlan:"TrainingsBLOC", kalBloc:"BLOC", umbenennen:"Rename",
